## Summary

Fixes orientation when modifying images with `EditImage` node. For formats like `webp` the exif metadata was stripped resulting in the output losing orientation. For other formats the orientation is reseted because graphicmagic's `autoOrient()` rotates the pixels on every execution, resulting in multiple rotations if the orientation metadata is unchanged for vertical images.

To test use following workflow and upload two images - one in each orientation - taken with your phone. After edit image step the output images should have the same orientation displayed as the input images. Change the format to `webp` in the edit image node and test again to confirm that it works the same

```json
