## Summary

This PR addresses two issues:

1) We sometimes displayed setup cards where user couldn't do anything with dead links - the links were accidental dead UX and in general we shouldn't ever display this, we should just apply nothing automatically and continue if this was to happen
<img width="1026" height="338" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64064584-3fa2-478c-9d9f-19685c178b4b" />

2) These were displayed because the agent didn't understand that some fixedCollections, like the filters/conditions on data tables require values, and empty array or leaving out the parameter wasn't allowed, as there were min / max required fields for those. Adjusted workflow-sdk to validate that, and to generate now type definitions like

```
/**
   * Filter to decide which rows get
   * @default {}
   */
  filters: {
    /** Conditions
     * @minItems 1
     */
    conditions: [
      {
        /** Choose from the list, or specify using an &lt;a href="https://docs.n8n.io/code/expressions/"&gt;expression&lt;/a&gt;
         * @loadOptionsMethod getDataTableColumns
         * @default id
         */
        keyName?: string | Expression<string>;
        /** Condition
         * @loadOptionsMethod getConditionsForColumn
         * @default eq
         */
        condition?: string | Expression<string>;
        /** Value
         * @displayOptions.hide { condition: ["isEmpty", "isNotEmpty", "isTrue", "isFalse"] }
         */
        keyValue?: string | Expression<string> | PlaceholderValue;
      },
      ...Array<{
        /** Choose from the list, or specify using an &lt;a href="https://docs.n8n.io/code/expressions/"&gt;expression&lt;/a&gt;
         * @loadOptionsMethod getDataTableColumns
         * @default id
         */
        keyName?: string | Expression<string>;
        /** Condition
         * @loadOptionsMethod getConditionsForColumn
         * @default eq
         */
        condition?: string | Expression<string>;
        /** Value
         * @displayOptions.hide { condition: ["isEmpty", "isNotEmpty", "isTrue", "isFalse"] }
         */
        keyValue?: string | Expression<string> | PlaceholderValue;
      }>,
    ];
  };
```

instead of optional `filters?` and `conditions?` fields without any hints on required `minItems`.

The agent still struggles to debug this, as it doesn't have a "validate workflow" tool, but at least this seems to guide it when it's modifying/creating workflows.

To test this I found that creating workflows with `Manual Trigger` and `Upsert Data Table` node manually without configuring them at all and asking the AI to complete setting them up would lead to these cases where it had to understand the conditions field of the upsert node correctly.

