## Summary

Fixes two silent failure modes in the workflow auto-deactivation notification path (`ExecutionRecoveryService.autoDeactivateWorkflowsIfNeeded`).

### Bug 1 — Push notification dropped when editor tab is already open

When a workflow is auto-deactivated (after N consecutive crashed executions), the in-app notification was delivered via:

```ts
this.push.once('editorUiConnected', async () => {
    await sleep(1000);
    this.push.broadcast({ type: 'workflowAutoDeactivated', data: { workflowId } });
});
```

`push.once('editorUiConnected', ...)` listens for the **next** connection event. If the user already had the n8n editor open in a browser tab, `editorUiConnected` never fires again for that session — so the `workflowAutoDeactivated` message was silently discarded and the user continued to see the workflow as `Active` until a manual reload.

**Fix:** call `push.broadcast()` immediately so all currently-open editor tabs are notified right away. The deferred `once` listener is retained **in addition** (not replaced) to handle the case where no browser has the editor open at the moment of deactivation.

```ts
// Notify editors that are currently open
this.push.broadcast({ type: 'workflowAutoDeactivated', data: { workflowId } });

// Also notify the next editor session that connects
this.push.once('editorUiConnected', async () => {
    await sleep(1000);
    this.push.broadcast({ type: 'workflowAutoDeactivated', data: { workflowId } });
});
```

### Bug 2 — Email send failure produces no log trace

`notifyWorkflowAutodeactivated()` returns `{ emailSent: boolean }` but the return value was discarded. When SMTP is not configured, `emailSent` is `false` — silently. There was no log entry indicating why the auto-deactivation email was never received, making it very hard to debug.

**Fix:** capture the return value and emit a `warn` log when `emailSent` is false, pointing explicitly to the missing SMTP configuration.

## Root cause (from issue)

A high-fan-out workflow (~2,000 items × 19 filter nodes = ~38,000 node executions) triggered repeated process crashes. The auto-deactivation safety mechanism fired correctly, but both notification paths (email and push) failed silently, leaving the user with no indication of what happened.

## Test plan

- [x] Open n8n editor with a workflow active
- [x] Trigger `autoDeactivateWorkflowsIfNeeded` (e.g. simulate N crashed executions)
- [x] Confirm `workflowAutoDeactivated` push event is received **without** closing and reopening the browser tab
- [x] Confirm a `warn` log line appears in server logs when SMTP is not configured
- [x] Confirm email is still sent when SMTP **is** configured (no regression)

Relates to: https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/28739

