## Summary

This PR adds a new Databricks node.

**Resources implemented:**

- **Databricks SQL** — Execute SQL statements against Databricks SQL warehouses. Handles async execution, polls for completion, fetches chunked result sets, and returns each row as a separate n8n item.
- **Unity Catalog** — Manage catalogs, schemas, tables, volumes, and functions via the Unity Catalog API (catalogs: CRUD; volumes: CRUD; tables: get/list; functions: create/delete/get/list).
- **Model Serving** — Query ML model serving endpoints. Auto-detects the endpoint's input format (chat, completions, embeddings, dataframe, etc.) from its OpenAPI schema and validates the request body, returning detailed errors with examples on mismatch.
- **Genie** — Interact with Databricks Genie AI spaces: start conversations, send messages, retrieve responses, and execute/fetch results of SQL queries attached to messages.
- **Files** — Upload (up to 5 GiB), download, delete, and get metadata for files in Unity Catalog volumes; also supports listing, creating, and deleting directories.
- **Vector Search** — Create, get, list, and query vector search indexes (Delta Sync and Direct Access index types).

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/50009c48-225b-4e9b-9508-51ebc269ff55

**Testability:**

1. Create a free trial account on [Databricks](https://www.databricks.com/)
2. Create an API token and save it to a credential
3. Play around with the node

