## Summary

The `delayedLoading` debounced function was recreated on every `fetchDataTables` call, preventing debouncing from working. Each call got its own timer instead of sharing one, causing the loading indicator to always show immediately rather than after 300ms.

**Before:**
```typescript
const fetchDataTables = async () => {
  const delayedLoading = debounce(() => {
    loading.value = true;
  }, 300);
  // ... rest of function
};
```

**After:**
```typescript
const delayedLoading = debounce(() => {
  loading.value = true;
}, 300);

const fetchDataTables = async () => {
  // ... rest of function
};
```

Moved `delayedLoading` to module scope so all `fetchDataTables` invocations share the same debounced timer.

