## Summary

Fixed error handling in the Asana node when "Continue On Fail" is enabled. Previously, error items were not being displayed correctly in the UI output panel

**Before:**
<img width="2409" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb4f2d21-c165-4e34-a208-3609947745e5" />

**After:**
<img width="2417" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58f5dea3-64c1-4a42-b301-03f865b7f3a4" />

## Root Cause Analysis

The Asana node's error handling was incorrectly structured. When `continueOnFail()` was enabled, the error was being pushed directly to `returnData` without wrapping it in the expected `INodeExecutionData` format:
```typescript
// Before
catch (error) {
  if (this.continueOnFail()) {
    returnData.push({ error: error.message });
    continue;
  }
  throw error;
}
```

n8n expects execution data items to have a `json` property containing the data. Without this wrapper, the UI could not properly parse and display the error output.

**Fix:**
```typescript
// After
if (this.continueOnFail()) {
  const executionErrorData = this.helpers.constructExecutionMetaData(
    this.helpers.returnJsonArray({ error: error.message }),
    { itemData: { item: i } },
  );
  returnData.push(...executionErrorData);
  continue;
}
throw error;
```

The fix:
1. Uses `this.helpers.returnJsonArray()` to properly wrap the error in the expected `json` structure
2. Uses `this.helpers.constructExecutionMetaData()` with `itemData` to maintain input-output item correlation

