## Summary

This pull request refactors how log entries are computed and updated in the `useLogsExecutionData` composable. The main improvement is switching from a computed property to a throttled watcher for updating log entries, which helps optimize performance when handling frequent changes in execution data.

**Performance and reactivity improvements:**

* Replaced the computed `entries` property with a ref and a `watchThrottled` function to update log entries, reducing unnecessary recalculations and improving responsiveness for large datasets. [[1]](diffhunk://#diff-2e219bd6dd78653c85243ea832be45a108b9ba2bc2731a05b59a34535b83b9ccL50-R52) [[2]](diffhunk://#diff-2e219bd6dd78653c85243ea832be45a108b9ba2bc2731a05b59a34535b83b9ccR88-R104)
* Imported `watchThrottled` from `@vueuse/core` to enable throttled updates, preventing excessive updates when dependencies change rapidly.

