## Summary
This PR adds basic Data Store page but more importantly, it expands our front-end module system by:
- Introducing module descriptions:
```typescript
export type ResourceMetadata = {
	key: string;
	displayName: string;
	i18nKeys?: Record<string, string>;
};

export type FrontendModuleDescription = {
	id: string;
	name: string;
	description: string;
	icon: string;
	routes?: RouteRecordRaw[];
	projectTabs?: {
		overview?: DynamicTabOptions[];
		project?: DynamicTabOptions[];
		shared?: DynamicTabOptions[];
	};
	resources?: ResourceMetadata[];
};
```
- Centralizing module init logic in `ModuleInitializer`. It registers custom components and routes from module descriptions (for now, all module descriptions are imported manually and module metadata from the description is not used but will serve as a foundation moving forward).
- Allowing modules to register custom resource that can be used in `ResourcesListLayout` component

TESTING NOTE: Until backend is merged, we need to mock API responses. Check [this comment](https://linear.app/n8n/issue/ADO-3839/fe-add-datastores-tab-to-project-and-overview-pages#comment-e469a9bb) for more details on how to test locally.

