## Summary

<!--
Describe what the PR does and how to test.
Photos and videos are recommended.
-->

Fix the retry logic when using "Retry On Error" in combination with "Continue" or "Continue (using error output)" option for "On Error" behavior. Before, if the first try was unsuccessful, it would try the max number of times and return the result of the first try (which is an error). This is because the data returned by the node was not updated in the retry loop. After this fix the node returns the data after the first successful try, and if none of them succeed, it returns the last error.

Workflow to manually try it out:
```json
{
  "name": "Retry and Continue On Fail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
