Improve the performance a little bit.
A better improvement would be a complete overhaul.
It is currently very slow.
Workflow without split: 4 sec returns 1000 rows
Workflow with splt: 9 sec returns each row (batch size 1).
Instead of passing only items to the next node, information about the start position and end position could be passed.
This way the data would not have to be physically copied.
But then you would have to adapt each node.

Another optimization would be a real loop.
But there you would have to completely rework the system that a node can output multiple data.
Instead of `return this.prepareOutputData([])` there should be a possibility to send the data: `this.pushOutput(index, this.prepareOutputData([]))`.
Or return a "Stream object".
```ts
    const streamObject = new ItemStream();
    streamObject.add(this.prepareOutputData([]));
    return streamObject;
```

The streamobject could also be async:

```ts
    //In node:
    const streamObject = new ItemStream();
    someHttpRequest.request(function(result) {
        streamObject.add(this.prepareOutputData([{json: {result: result}}]));
    });
    return streamObject;
```

this procedure would also benefit the if and switch node

