## Introduction

This PR implements and expands on [the 2020 MLH Fellowship's proposal on node error handling](https://hackmd.io/@jh6EYijgQ-GeAm9l3y-a4g/rksOxZkfv). This proposal standardizes access to the **status code** and **error message** in the API response error object on a per-node basis, 

## Original Proposal

Instead of sequential access checks for properties in the API response error object...

```ts
if (error.response && error.response.body && error.response.body.message) {
    // Try to return the error prettier
    throw new Error(`Spotify error response [${error.statusCode}]: ${error.response.body.message}`);
}
```

The original proposal maps the paths to them:

```ts
const box2ToN8nErrorAPITransformer: N8nErrorAPI = {
    code: ["error", "error", "status"],
    message: ["error", "error", "message"]
};
```

And handles/rethrows the error from a centralized location:

```ts
// GenericFunctions.ts (node-specific)
const errorObj = errorHandler(error, box2ToN8nErrorAPITransformer);
userDisplayNodeError("Spotify", errorObj.code, errorObj.message);

// centralized location
const recursivelyFindAction = (accumulator, currentValue) => accumulator[currentValue];

/**
* Takes in any API's error response object and uses the provided API to n8n Error Transformer to generate an n8n standard formatted error object.
* @param errorObj {any} - The API's Error Response Object
* @param pathTransformer {N8nErrorAPI} - The paths to parse in the errorObj to fetch the correct values.
* @return {N8nErrorAPIResponse} - The n8n standard API error object
*/
export const errorHandler = (errorObj: object, pathTransformer: N8nErrorAPI): N8nErrorAPIResponse => {
  const apiStandard: N8nErrorAPIResponse = {code: '', message: ''};

  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(pathTransformer)) {
    apiStandard[key] = value.reduce(recursivelyFindAction, errorObj).toString();
  }

  return apiStandard;
};

const userDisplayNodeError = (nodeName: string, statusCode: string, errorMessage: string): string => {
	throw new Error(`${nodeName} error response [${statusCode}]: ${errorMessage}`);
};
```

The property access syntax logic is similar to [Lodash's _.get](https://lodash.com/docs/4.17.15#get)).

## Expanded Proposal

In this implementation, a number of changes were introduced to the original proposal.

Functions and interfaces are renamed more explicitly:

```ts
export interface IN8nErrorPathMapping {
	[key: string]: string[];
	code: string[];
	message: string[];
}

export interface IN8nApiResponseError {
	[key: string]: string;
	code: string;
	message: string;
}
```

Error handling logic is refactored as a single operation; some typings are tightened. Note the `never` type should be used for [functions that do not return](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/basic-types.html#never). 

```ts
/**
 * Standardizes an API response error and throws it.
 *
 * @export
 * @param {string} nodeName
 * @param {object} errorObject
 * @param {IN8nErrorPathMapping} errorPathMapping
 * @returns {never}
 */
export function handleError(
	nodeName: string,
	errorObject: object,
	errorPathMapping: IN8nErrorPathMapping
): never {
	const apiResponseError = standardizeError(errorObject, errorPathMapping);
	throwApiResponseError(nodeName, apiResponseError);
}

/**
 * Converts an API error object into a standard N8N error object based on the error path mapping provided.
 *
 * @export
 * @param {object} errorObject
 * @param {IN8nErrorPathMapping} errorPathMapping
 * @returns {IN8nApiResponseError}
 */
function standardizeError(errorObject: object, errorPathMapping: IN8nErrorPathMapping): IN8nApiResponseError {
	const apiResponseError: IN8nApiResponseError = {
		code: '',
		message: '',
	};

	const findValueRecursively = (accumulator: any, currentValue: any) => accumulator[currentValue];

	Object.entries(errorPathMapping).forEach(([key, path]) => {
		apiResponseError[key] = path.reduce(findValueRecursively, errorObject).toString();
	});

	return apiResponseError;
};

/**
 * Throws an error with a standard N8N error message.
 *
 * @export
 * @param {string} nodeName
 * @param {IN8nApiResponseError} apiResponseError
 * @returns {never}
 */
function throwApiResponseError(
	nodeName: string,
	apiResponseError: IN8nApiResponseError,
): never {
	throw new Error(`${nodeName} error response [${apiResponseError.code}]: ${apiResponseError.message}`);
};
```

End result at call site:

```ts
try {
	return await this.helpers.request!(options);
} catch (error) {

	const errorPathMapping: IN8nErrorPathMapping = {
		code: ["error", "status"],
		message: ["error", "error"],
	};

	handleError("Hacker News", error, errorPathMapping);
}
```

## Implementation

The PR implements the expanded proposal in...
- the Hacker News node,
- the Spotify node, and
- the G Suite Admin node.

In all three cases, the new error-handling style **worked well** and was relatively quick to implement. Identifying the paths and verifying that they are correct is the only slightly time-consuming step.

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/44588767/103697082-2dee5600-4f7e-11eb-8ddb-4f6b2780f7a0.png)

![spotify_error](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/44588767/103808383-aadd0680-5036-11eb-9c62-9c51d3a4d67e.png)

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/44588767/103808461-c7793e80-5036-11eb-95d6-ed6b7590624b.png)

## Limitations

This proposal works well for those nodes that rely on a long chain of sequential access checks—a majority of all nodes. However, other error-handling patterns, such as those below, are not natively compatible with the proposal.

| Compatible? | Amount | Percentage |
|-------------|--------|------------|
| Yes         | 3      | 2%         |
| Likely      | 98     | 66%        |
| Maybe       | 29     | 20%        |
| Unlikely    | 3      | 2%         |
| Unknown     | 15     | 10%        |

_For the full breakdown, see the [next comment](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/1309#issuecomment-755560062)._

We could look into whether it is possible to adjust the proposal for these other cases:
- multiple error paths possible,
- multiple errors joined together,
- non-REST API implementations, and
- miscellaneous error-handling variants.

### Multiple error paths possible

Nodes: HubSpot, Toggl, etc.

```ts
} catch (error) {
	if (error.statusCode === 403) {
		throw new Error('The Toggle credentials are probably invalid!');
	}

	const errorMessage = error.response.body && (error.response.body.message || error.response.body.Message);
	if (errorMessage !== undefined) {
		throw new Error(errorMessage);
	}

	throw error;
}
```

### Multiple errors joined together

Nodes: Strapi, Strava, Twake, etc.

```ts
} catch (error) {
	if (error.response && error.response.body && error.response.body.message) {

		let messages = error.response.body.message;

		if (Array.isArray(error.response.body.message)) {
			messages = messages[0].messages.map((e: IDataObject) => e.message).join('|');
		}
		// Try to return the error prettier
		throw new Error(
			`Strapi error response [${error.statusCode}]: ${messages}`,
		);
	}
	throw error;
}
```

### Non-REST API implementations

Nodes: Slack, Humantic AI, SMS77, etc.

```ts
	if (response.ok === false) {
		throw new Error('Slack error response: ' + JSON.stringify(response));
	}

	return response;
} catch (error) {
	if (error.statusCode === 401) {
		// Return a clear error
		throw new Error('The Slack credentials are not valid!');
	}

	if (error.response && error.response.body && error.response.body.message) {
		// Try to return the error prettier
		throw new Error(`Slack error response [${error.statusCode}]: ${error.response.body.message}`);
	}

	// If that data does not exist for some reason return the actual error
	throw error;
}
```

### Miscellaneous error-handling variants

Nodes: PayPal, SalesForce, Shopify, etc.

```ts
} catch (error) {

	if (error.response.body) {
		let errorMessage = error.response.body.message;
		if (error.response.body.details) {
			errorMessage += ` - Details: ${JSON.stringify(error.response.body.details)}`;
		}
		throw new Error(errorMessage);
	}

	throw error;
}
```

## Open Questions

In order of importance:

- Is it possible to adjust the error-handling proposal to cover the "Maybe" and "Unknown" cases?
- Where should we place `IN8nErrorPathMapping` and `IN8nApiResponseError`? The path in this PR `packages/workflow/src/Interfaces.ts` is just a provisional location.
- Where should we place the error handling functionality? The path in this PR `packages/core/src/NodeExecutionFunctions.ts` is just a provisional location.
- Is there a way to "auto-discover" the API response error object's structure so as to auto-generate the error path mapping?
- How should we properly type the parameters in `findValueRecursively`?

